maria.chen: Quick sync — SDK error ergonomics. We're still seeing inconsistent error shapes across Python/TS and vague retry guidance from the API responses. Can we agree on a minimal structured error schema and typed exceptions in SDKs? :thinking:
kevin: +1 we get a lot of support tickets where people retry on 401/403 or swallow 429 incorrectly. My takeaway: typed exceptions + a top-level `retryable` flag would help a lot.
ash_winchester: I agree. Also separate `user_message` (friendly) from `developer_message` (debug info). Stable machine-readable `error_code` string is key.
danielle: Question: do we mirror HTTP status into `error_code` (e.g. `http.401`) or use semantic codes like `auth.invalid_api_key`? I lean semantic with an explicit `http_status` field.
kevin: Prefer semantic codes. Proposal (example JSON payload):
```json
{
  "error_code": "auth.invalid_api_key",
  "http_status": 401,
  "retryable": false,
  "user_message": "Invalid API key. Check your credentials.",
  "developer_message": "Key expired at 2026-03-10T12:04:55Z (request_id: abc123)",
  "meta": { "request_id": "abc123" }
}
```
Also expose typed exceptions in SDKs, e.g. `UnauthorizedError`, `RateLimitedError(retry_after_seconds)`.
maria.chen: Implementation notes: TS/JS SDK should throw error classes extending `RedwoodError` with fields `{ code, retryable, retryAfterSeconds, meta }`. Python should have specific exception classes with the same properties so catching is consistent.
deploy-bot: deploy-bot: CI: branch `sdk-error-schema` pushed, tests queued — https://ci.internal/7862 :robot_face:
nash_winchester: Edge cases: 502/503 should be retryable with backoff, but we must be careful about non-idempotent endpoints. Maybe include `retry_policy`: "always" | "idempotent_only" | "never"?
danielle: To keep SDK logic simple let's start with `retryable` (bool) + optional `retry_after_seconds` + a separate `idempotency_required` boolean on endpoint metadata (docs/sample apps can show examples). Also update sample apps to show how to surface `user_message` to end-users safely.
kevin: Action items: 1) Draft RFC for error schema + SDK examples (maria). 2) Server-side mapping layer to normalize legacy HTTP -> new schema (ash_winchester). 3) Update onboarding sample apps and docs (danielle). 4) Add SDK tests for typed exceptions and backwards compat (kevin). I'll open GH issues and link them.
maria.chen: I'll draft the RFC by EOW and include concrete Python/TS snippets and migration guidance. tagging @kevin @ash_winchester @danielle.
kevin: Sounds good, thanks. :thumbsup:
danielle: +1 — will prep a sample app PR template showing how to handle `user_message` vs `developer_message`. :raised_hands:
kevin: Quick example for TS throwing class:```ts
class RedwoodError extends Error {
  code: string;
  retryable: boolean;
  retryAfterSeconds?: number;
  constructor(payload) {
    super(payload.developer_message || payload.user_message);
    this.code = payload.error_code;
    this.retryable = payload.retryable;
    this.retryAfterSeconds = payload.retry_after_seconds;
  }
}
```
maria.chen: Great snippet — includes everything we'll need for docs. Let's avoid auto-retrying in SDKs unless `retryable === true` and endpoint marked idempotent or client explicitly opts in.
kevin: I'll track compat tests to ensure older clients that expect string messages keep them via `error.message` until we cut a major.
nash_winchester: Once RFC is up I'll start the server mapping and add a middleware that injects `request_id` into `meta`.
kevin: I'll create the GH epic and assign tasks. Thanks everyone.
